<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">756 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">756 CE in world history: 5 events, 1 birth, 5 deaths, 2 states founded and 1 that came to an end. 281 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/739">739 CE</a><a href="/years/744">744 CE</a><a href="/years/750">750 CE</a><a href="/years/751">751 CE</a><a href="/years/756" aria-current="page">756 CE</a><a href="/years/757">757 CE</a><a href="/years/763">763 CE</a><a href="/years/768">768 CE</a><a href="/years/778">778 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/an-lushan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-5">5 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">An Lushan proclaims himself emperor of Yan at Luoyang</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The rebel Tang general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan">An Lushan</a> declared himself emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> on the Lunar New Year, founding the state of Yan, and named Zhang Tongru and the surrendered Tang official Daxi Xun his chancellors. Yan collapsed in 763.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan">An Lushan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-15">15 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mutinous guards kill the chancellor Yang Guozhong at Mawei</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">When the imperial party fleeing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a> stopped at Mawei Station, guard soldiers blaming the chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-guozhong">Yang Guozhong</a> for the chaos killed him and his family. Emperor Xuanzong was forced to order the death of his consort Yang Guifei.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-guozhong">Yang Guozhong</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/donation-of-pepin" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/donation-of-pepin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/donation-of-pepin">Donation of Pepin</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Donation of Pepin was the grant by the Frankish king Pepin the Short to the papacy of lands in central Italy taken from the Lombards, promised in 754 and carried out in 756.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-musara">Battle of Musara</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Musara was fought in May 756 on the banks of the Guadalquivir near Córdoba.</p></div></li></ol></section>
